## Conclusion
Lowering machine load cleared exactly ONE of 49 failures. The remaining 48 are
REPRODUCIBLE AT LOW LOAD, i.e. NOT environmental. Composition: 41 are followed
by a timeout marker; 31 carry real `expect()` assertion errors (sets overlap).

This REFUTES the earlier claim that the Stage 4 failures were mainly
high-load timeouts. The executing agent's census ({ASSERT:25, TIMEOUT:24}) was
right; my two intermediate summaries were wrong both times.

