## Verification of the deduped failure list (by the coordinator)
`dc-warn/out/stage4-attribution/failures-lowload-unique.txt` (48 names) was compared
against an independently derived dedup of the same stdout:
    only-in-agent: 0   only-in-my-list: 0   common: 48
-> the extraction is verified correct.

Note for anyone reproducing this comparison: use `LC_ALL=C`, and remember that
`sed 's/^(fail) //'` (BRE) is the correct form — an unescaped-paren pattern
silently fails to strip the prefix and makes two identical sets look disjoint.
Two of my intermediate comparisons reported a false "REAL DIFFERENCE" for
exactly that reason; the sets were identical throughout.
